{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Enlarge [your tent].</b> The sense of \"Enlarge [the] place\" is on account of the multitude of children." "<b>Stretch out.</b> [It] returns to the children of the desolate one, or the word \"stretching\" is missing, like \"and he said to Joseph\" (Genesis 48:1)." "And the sense of <b>do not hold back</b> is like \"do not withhold them\" — let the curtains of your tent stretch out." "<b>Your cords.</b> The cords of the tent. Now behold the sense is the towns and villages."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:28.586908697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}